From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Sep 30 16:45:31 1997
From: Guy Dallaire <gdallaire () gustave ! revenu ! gouv ! qc ! ca>
Date: Tue, 30 Sep 1997 16:45:31 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMM: Can an AlphaServer 1000 do more than 640x480 pixels
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078617110678

First, let me thank averybody who quickly responded.

The answer is NO. The built-in VGA chip in the AlphaServer 1000 is VERY 
SLOW and cannot do more than 640x480 with the current driver.

Most of you suggested that we buy a High Performance PCI graphics adapter 
and disable the built-in VGA adapter with ECU prior to installing the new 
PCI board. While the adapter is disabled, do not forget to set 
console=serial at the SRM prompt before booting the machine !

An alternative is to use a serial console and an X workstation or emulator 
to do some X stuff with the server.

