Hello Managers,

My original question was :
----------
"
We have recently installed DU 4.0b and Netscape Enterprise Server as our
web server.
Our problem is :
When the server starts , everything goes fine but after 3-4 hours, we could
not access the pages. It gives FORBIDDEN message.
Here are some entries from the error log file:
append-trailer reports: error opening buffer from 
/usr/users/webadmin/ns-home/docs/index.html (Not enough space)

Why does it say "Not Enough Space"?  I checked the disk , our disk is not
full, swap space is also OK.
"
-----

The following people responded to my question:

Brian C Hill <bchill@bch.net>
"Christopher L. Davis" <cld@prin.edu>
"Pam Woods, Systems Manager" <axsymgr@UAA.ALASKA.EDU>
"David B. Ritch" <dbritch@earthlink.net>
Knut Hellebx <Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com>
K.McManus@greenwich.ac.uk
Graham Allan <ALLAN@mnhep1.hep.umn.edu>

I added the following entry to /etc/sysconfigtab file and reboot.
vm:
        vm-mapentries = 20000

My problem is now solved. Thanks to all people who sent messages for the
solution.

Also, Graham Allan sent the following address which describes several
other solutions.
http://www.digital.com/internet/document/ias/tuning.html 

Thanks all.

Zehra Soysert
UNIX System Administrator
Ege University,Izmir-Turkey

