> My original questio/problem:
> 
> I am using Media Robot Utility 1.0 on DU 3.2G. with a TL894 (boy, is
> it slick).
> 
> I am using the presupplied barcodes and this makes inventory quick,
> but is there a way through MRU to get it to show me the bar codes
> numbers?
> 
> 
> I.E.  
> 
> (arthur)# robot show slots
> SLOT:           0               Full
> SLOT:           1               Full
> SLOT:           2               Full
> SLOT:           3               Full
> SLOT:           4               Full
> SLOT:           5               Full
> 
> etc.
> 
> The man pages explain that there is a way (if your library supports
> them) to read the barcodes into NVRAM.  The TL894 does support the
> barcodes, but I can't figure out how to read them into MRU.
> 
> TIA
> 
> (And yes, I will be upgrading to MRU 1.1 after I upgrade to DU 4.0b in
> a few months)
> 
> 
> The solution was VERY obvious, but very well hidden.
> 
> Version 1.0 of the MRU DOES support Bar Codes, the TL894 emulates the
> TL810 as far as the MRU is concerned, and DOES support bar codes. The
> problem lies in the documentation for the set up of the TL894.
> 
> It says that there is an option (with the TL894 setup) under
> configuration, called "No Bar Code Scan" It's tucked away, and not
> documented well.  Anyway. If this is disabled, that Bar Codes ARE
> reflected. If it is enabled, than bar codes are NOT reflected in MRU.
> 
> 
> A bit backward, but aren't we all.
> 
> 
> Well, it's late. I am here late on another Saturday night. Not DEC,
> just us.
> Life of a Sys Admin. No sleep, lots of coffee, and my wife is mad
> (that I'm working another Saturday night).
> 
> Best to all
> 
> 
> From the dark land of the mole people
