Hello managers,

I appreciate the response to this problem I posted yesterday. I'll
detail the problem and solution below:


Problem:

I'm trying to use Hummingbird Exceed on my Windows NT workstation to
connect to a Digital UNIX 3.2d server and get a full screen session
using xdmcp query mode.

My first attempt at doing this produced the message "fatal error - xdm
session declined".

After clearing the xdm key field in Exceed, I was able to get the xdm
logon screen to come up. However after logging in I get the message
"Cannot start session manager from remote client - access denied."


Solution:

Clear the xdm "key" field on the Exceed side, and enable the "Allow
clients To Modify Host Access Control List" setting in Exceed's XConfig
program, security options.


