Subject: Re:  CDE Hangs
Status: RO

Been there.  A supposed feature of CDE is that it is "network aware".  But
it is entirely too network aware for its own good, since the slightest
change to the network configuration causes the problem you're seeing.
I'm lead to believe (and so far agree) that the solution is to add a
line "export DTNONETWORK=true" to /.dtprofile, logout, log back in and
then make the network changes.  You'll have to change the network
configuration back to do this.  This changes make it network-unaware
for the duration of the change.  You can undo the change when it is
complete and stable.

So the steps are:

1.  Boot to single user and restore the old network configuration.
2.  Reboot or continue to multi-user.
3.  Login, change /.dtprofile and logout.
4.  Login, change the network configuration, cycle through single
    user or reboot.
5.  Login, unchange /.dtprofile and continue.

There may be a release note on the supposed feature.
