Subject: FW: Raw Partitions for Sybase
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078617110366

Graham,
                We are running Sybase on raw. All you need is a device in the
/dev directory pointing to the raw disk. You can test this by using the dd
command to see if you can write the data to the disk. Sybase will take the raw
device you specify and divide the disk up.

                You need to add this to your sysconfigtab and reboot your
system. You current problem sounds like the max-proc setting.
                pts:
                        nptys = 512
                proc:
                                max-proc-per-user = 256
                        max-threads-per-user = 1024

                You also need to make sure that you added the devices in order.
If you skip devices it will not use the ones you added. I also changed maxusers
in the kernel from 32 to 512. You can create a script that telnets in a loop so
that you can simulate users login into the system.

                We had the same problem with our keyboard using the cybex switch
boxes. I plugged a DEC keyboard and mouse into straight into the system and the
problem went away.

Thanks,
          Brian


