From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Sep 03 04:25:19 1997
From: mortimer () physics ! uq ! edu ! au
Date: Wed, 03 Sep 1997 04:25:19 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Nag and loader problem after Fortran upgrade.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078617110202

Hi DU Admins

My question was about a problem with the Nag shared libraries
after an upgrade of Fortran from 3.7 to 4.1 on alphas running
DU 3.2g.

I didn't get any replies which was no surprise since it was 
such a strange problem.  I'm posting a summary anyway just
in case anyone else ever gets caught by this.

I got the solution from Nag.  There's a bug in their script
for building the shared libraries.  They sent me a patch and
it works.

The mystery about this - both to me and to Nag - is why the buggy 
shared libraries ever worked and why they continued to work under
DU 4.0[bc] but not under 3.2g after the Fortran upgrade.


Ian

